  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Mandatory National Service at 18; tougher sentences (including whole‑life terms), 8,000 more neighbourhood police, facial recognition, four new prisons; monthly Rwanda removals, asylum treaty rewrite, a falling legal annual migration cap, higher visa fees/health checks; defence to 2.5% of GDP and a Veterans’ Bill; NI cuts and abolition of main self‑employed NI, 10‑point SME plan, extend full expensing, fraud bill, tougher welfare sanctions, prompt‑payment enforcement; NHS funding above inflation with major recruitment, Pharmacy First, women’s health strategy, dental recovery, Tobacco & Vapes Bill; clarify biological sex in the Equality Act and protect single‑sex spaces. TEXT_E: Neighbourhood Policing Guarantee, knife bans, prison capacity, Border Security Command, uphold ECHR; New Deal for Working People (day‑one rights, ban exploitative zero‑hours/fire‑and‑rehire, minimum wage on living costs), Race Equality Act, pay‑gap reporting, conversion‑ban, modernised gender recognition law, votes at 16; zero‑carbon electricity by 2030, Warm Homes Plan, restore nature/clean rivers, tougher water regulation, animal welfare, broad public‑health restrictions; major NHS/social‑care/mental‑health expansions, free breakfast clubs, more teachers and nurseries; fiscal rules to balance the current budget and get debt falling, corporation‑tax cap at 25% with full expensing, replace business rates.",
